Feature: EN 1996 check outcome of committed documents
  A committed before-snapshot of the mutation fixtures is evaluated by the production report and by the independent per-wall utilisations of `../../🔮️oracles/🚦️check-outcome/🐍️.py` (compression, mid-height, slenderness and simplified method as the worst row over the load cases; declared eccentricity, shear and sliding, lateral flexure and concentrated load per load case; fire thickness, chases, movement joints, openings with lintels, reinforced masonry, bar layout and the floor diaphragm classification of the detailing documents `detail-rich-pass` and `detail-rich-fail`, the diaphragm displacement ratio from a PyNite shear-beam analogy).
  Each row names one check id, its status (pass at a utilisation of at most 1, fail above 1) and its utilisation; rows were picked away from the near-limit band so the status is unambiguous.

